    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/guianacara-dacrya-3/",
      "html": "<p>The genus Guianacara currently comprises seven described species, all of which originate from the Guiana shield in South America. Guianacara dacrya was described in 2011 and originates from the tributaries of the rivers Rio Branco and Essequibo.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/guianacara-dacrya-3/",
      "html": "<p>Guianacara are high backed, medium sized cichlids (12-15 cm), which reproduce as cave breeders with parent family. For cichlid conditions they can be considered peaceful, as cave breeders they do not dig excessively and plant food is not on their menu. This makes them ideal cichlids for larger community aquariums.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/guianacara-dacrya-3/",
      "html": "<p>They reproduce as cave breeders with parent family.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/guianacara-dacrya-3/",
      "html": "<p>The genus was only established in 1989 and only one species – G. geayi – was known before; Pellegrin described it in 1909. From this one can already conclude that the species look quite similar. Before the genus Guianacara was established, G. geayi was listed in the genera Aequidens and Acarichthys. Apart from minor anatomical differences, the species differ mainly in their colouring. This makes determination quite difficult, because there are only a few cichlids that change their coloration as drastically as the Guianacara species, and that within seconds. Identification of captive G. dacrya was nevertheless easy, because they are bred ones and the breeders usually know exactly which species they are looking after.</p>"
    }
  ],
